+// Whether a refresh asked for after a reply (nothing in flight) fires at
+// once (the default) or a frame after the reply (the M2 behaviour,
+// PS5WK_WC_REFRESH_NOW=0). An update asked for just after a reply (a wheel
+// event or a timer that came in then) started a full frame later and was
+// shown a frame later than it could be; and with a frame of the title's
+// already under way for video or animations, it missed that frame too. The
+// title still paces updates to the display: its frame's first draw waits
+// for the previous swap's flip, and the reply goes after the swap.
+static bool refreshAtOnceAfterReply()
+{
+    static const bool atOnce = [] {
+        const char* text = getenv("PS5WK_WC_REFRESH_NOW");
+        return !text || strcmp(text, "0");
+    }();
+    return atOnce;
+}
